    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="0714" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/910: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Representative on the Inter-Allied Committee</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Charles H. Smithy</hi>)<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d585-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-26T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1919,
                                12 noon.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to arrangement between Stevens and Nagao relative to standardizing
                    gauge of railway between Changchun and Harbin, provided the Russian authorities
                    have no objection thereto. Please confer with Mr. Stevens and with Mr. Morris on
                    his return and say that this Government cannot approve any such change, except
                    it be decided by agreement with some duly constituted Russian Government
                    recognized by the Associated Governments.</p>
                <p>The Department does not wish to embarrass Mr. Stevens in his having reached a
                    working agreement with Japan, but believes it necessary to point out that this
                    Government interprets “The Russian authorities” referred to in the memorandum
                    drawn up by Mr. Stevens and Mr. Nagao,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d585-f2"/> to mean
                    a duly constituted Russian Government recognized by the Associated
                    Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d585-f1" n="32" type="source" xml:id="d585-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Consul at Vladivostok.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d585-f2" n="33" xml:id="d585-f2-content">
                <p>See memorandum of Nagao printed as a subenclosure, <ref target="#pg609">p.
                        609</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
